From 181bbdf4b33b856c50176408b3b5e029f0ec71de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:45:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] rtems-esp-wifi: share C3 modem startup and PHY with
 Bluetooth

Consolidated from the following downstream patches. Original rationale
and provenance are retained below; source licensing is unchanged.

Original-patch: 0015-share-phy-ownership-with-bluetooth.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-20T04:45:28+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: 732a5c70afb40868cc6835fdeddd852b3a0e27e0

Share modem startup and PHY ownership with Bluetooth

Follow ESP-IDF's per-modem PHY ownership and PLL tracking. Prepare common
radio memory, clocks and coexistence once so either radio can start first.
Keep the BT peripheral enabled across PHY calibration, and expose IDF's
complete BT peripheral reset including its low-power clock block.

Original-patch: 0016-align-c3-radio-power-domain-startup.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-20T04:45:28+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: 732a5c70afb40868cc6835fdeddd852b3a0e27e0

Match ESP-IDF C3 radio power-domain startup

Direct boot skips rtc_init(), which clears force-up and force-no-isolation
bits before the radio takes ownership. Do not force the Wi-Fi/BT domains
on or repeat the BSP's extra BT clock/reset sequence. Release BT isolation
before preparing the shared modem domain, as esp_bt_power_domain_on() does.

Original-patch: 0017-match-wifi-sleep-clock-calibration-abi.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-20T04:45:28+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: 732a5c70afb40868cc6835fdeddd852b3a0e27e0

Match the Wi-Fi sleep-clock calibration ABI

The Wi-Fi OS adapter expects Q12 microseconds, not the system RTC's Q19.
On C3, follow the selected Bluetooth LP clock: XTAL is divided to 1 MHz.
Allow the application to provide its measured RTC frequency for modem sleep
instead of relying on a nominal oscillator frequency.
